    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (77.42) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56). **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a massive SP matchup advantage against Robert Gasser, whose xERA of 5.63 provides an ideal environment for him to deliver in the heart of the order. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizes on a strong platoon edge against a hittable arm in Holmes, as his aggressive positioning at the #2 spot maximizes his exposure to run-scoring opportunities. We are also leaning on **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) and **Josh Jung** (64.46) to provide steady production; **Sam Antonacci** particularly stands out as a core play given his leadoff assignment and favorable wind conditions that boost his base projections.\n\nThe toughest decision of the day involved **Nolan Schanuel** (44.77), who narrowly missed the starting cut. While his potential #3 spot is enviable, the optimizer ultimately penalized him heavily for a daunting matchup against Nathan Eovaldi, whose 3.19 xERA suppresses offensive output significantly. Conversely, we are keeping **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.93) in the UTIL slot despite a difficult draw against Skenes, banking on his elite talent to offset the pitcher\u2019s dominance, though his score remains marginal compared to the high-upside plays elsewhere.\n\nManagers should monitor the status of **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Josh Jung**, as all remain dependent on \"Lineup Pending\" status; any shift in their projected batting order could compress their efficiency scores. While we remain bolstered by depth, the absence of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** continues to limit our flexibility in chasing SB\u2014our scarcest category. We are relying on the speed profiles of **Nasim Nunez** and the rest of the active roster to bridge that gap today, keeping a close eye on the wind reports at the stadium as they provide a subtle boost for **Miguel Vargas** and **Sam Antonacci**.",
